+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry owns input validation so every executor receives input accepted by its registered JSON Schema.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `execute` rejects missing required properties, wrong types and invalid enum members before invoking an executor, returns a corrective `ToolResponse` naming the property path and failed constraint without values in results or logs, passes valid input including unknown properties unchanged exactly once without defaults or coercion, and preserves the `Unknown tool: <name>` exception for unregistered names ([validated by: rejects malformed input privately and passes accepted input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L19)).
+- Static schemas compile at registration, invalid schemas throw an error naming the tool at registration, and ten subsequent executions reuse the compiled schema without reading it again ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- Function-valued definitions resolve at execution time and validate against the current schema, caching compilation by resolved schema object rather than tool name ([validated by: validates dynamic definitions against the current schema and caches each schema object](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L99)).
+
+## Integration and release
+
+The returned rejection uses the existing tool-result conversation path, allowing the model to correct a call within the existing tool-round bound. Executor exceptions are outside the input-validation contract.
+
+Implementation also updates README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md, adds the validator as a runtime dependency, points the one-line execute comment here, and publishes a MINOR migration note in CHANGELOG.md and the PR description explaining that executors no longer receive malformed input.
diff --git a/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts b/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts
